; Regression: when a line terminator ended an interpolation (and its string; grammar.md
; §4.2), a `(`, `[` or `{` opened inside the interpolation stayed open in the parser, which
; then swallowed the following declarations into it (newlines are insignificant inside
; parentheses). The interpolation ends at the line terminator: its open delimiters are
; unclosed (K0101 at each opener) and the next line parses normally.
(SourceFile
  (FieldDecl let a = (StringLit (Interpolation (ParenExpr (NameExpr a)))))
  (FieldDecl let b = (StringLit (Interpolation (CallExpr (NameExpr f) (ArgList (Arg (NameExpr x)))))))
  (FieldDecl let c = (StringLit (Interpolation (ListExpr (NameExpr x)))))
  (FieldDecl let d = (StringLit (Interpolation (LambdaExpr (NameExpr x)))))
  (FieldDecl let e = (Literal 1)))
